ricepilot doctor: 1 problem. nothing was changed; the commands are for you to run.

PROBLEM 1 of 1: <HOME>/.config/hypr
  is empty, and the directory you adopted from here is in the attic.
  rule: D49 (`rollback` does not undo an `adopt`)

  `ricepilot adopt` (id <TS>) moved your directory from here to the attic
  and linked this path into profile `mine`. a rollback since then retired
  that link, which leaves the path empty; it does not put the directory
  back.

  your directory is still at
    <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/attic/<TS><HOME>/.config/hypr

  moved back, it is a real directory again. profile `mine` still declares
  this path, so a later `ricepilot switch mine` refuses it rather than
  re-linking over it — the safe way round.

  run:
    # your own directory, back where it was
    mv -nT <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/attic/<TS><HOME>/.config/hypr <HOME>/.config/hypr
    # or, instead, link the copy in profile `mine` again
    ricepilot switch mine --commit

